# SNS Growth Bridge Cursor Rules

Before editing code, read:

- `AGENTS.md`
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/CONTRACTS.md`
- `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`
- `docs/CURSOR_AGENT_IMPLEMENTATION.md`

## Core intent

This repository is a shared growth-intelligence layer between two separate products:

- My-SNS: creator-facing SaaS and publishing source of truth
- SNS-AI: autonomous/operator growth engine

Do not merge their applications or runtime state.

## Always preserve

- My-SNS owns OAuth, publish jobs, publish attempts, approval revisions, workspace/auth.
- SNS-AI owns its manual-only/autopilot runtime state and operator workflows.
- Bridge owns contracts, adapters, scoring, strategy logic, fixtures, compatibility tests.
- Human-correction evidence and audience-performance evidence are separate signal families.
- Creator hard constraints outrank performance optimization.

## Never do automatically

- enable SNS-AI accounts
- restore schedules or cron triggers in SNS-AI
- publish to a provider
- send replies/DMs
- copy provider credentials
- introduce a third publishing queue
- create a shared production database during v1
- delete source-repo learning code before parity tests
- make cross-repository production changes during Phase 0

## Implementation style

- pure functions before I/O
- strict TypeScript in Bridge
- runtime-validated versioned contracts
- deterministic fixtures
- fail closed on unsupported schema / ambiguous identity / invalid metrics
- record source commit SHAs in audit docs
- keep PRs small and phase-scoped

## Required first task

If `docs/audit/MY_SNS_CURRENT_STATE.md`, `docs/audit/SNS_AI_CURRENT_STATE.md`, and `docs/audit/MAPPING_MATRIX.md` do not exist, perform Phase 0 only. Do not start package implementation in the same change unless the audit contains no unresolved mapping blockers and the human explicitly requested implementation beyond Phase 0.
